{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The rider's own trace measurement is established, but it is not a MATERIAL deviation, and the consequences that would follow from materiality do not. The governing figure under POL-RD-01 is gps_trace.trace_distance_km = 14.12 km against a booked optimal of 10.8 km, an excess of 3.32 km, or 30.74%. The billed figure (trip_record.actual_distance_km = 14.1 km) puts the excess in the same band (3.3 km, 30.6%), so the two distance fields do not straddle any threshold and the finding is stable whichever is read. Both sit below POL-RD-01's materiality gates of more than 50% of the optimal distance and more than 8.0 km absolute, so no material deviation is recorded, POL-RD-06 is not engaged on materiality, and neither a FULL_REFUND uplift nor a driver-conduct referral is available on this record.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-03205", "EV-TRIP-03205"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01", "POL-RD-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Even if the driver_profile is consulted, POL-RD-06's pattern test is not met and none of its three effects can fire. driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 1, below the threshold of 3, and 1 divided by driver_profile.completed_trips_90d (172) is 0.006, far below 0.05. The lifetime counter prior_deviation_flags on the same artifact is not the trailing-90-day field POL-RD-06 names, and POL-GEN-01 forbids substituting one for the other. There is therefore no basis to resolve a balanced record in the rider's favour, no FULL_REFUND uplift and no conduct referral, and the evidence here is not balanced in any event because the trace is complete and no counter-artifact has been produced.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-03205"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's monetary recovery, if any refund is due at all, is fixed by the POL-RD-02 arithmetic on this METERED fare and is SGD 3.55, not the SGD 6.50 claimed. recomputed_fare = (3.80 + 0.75 x 10.8 + 0.28 x 14.6) x surge 1.0 + 0.80 platform fee = 16.788; refund = charged_total 20.30 less 16.788 = 3.512, rounded UP to the nearest SGD 0.05 = 3.55. The claim overstates the policy figure by nearly a factor of two. The refund is also only 17.3% of charged_total, far below the 90% full-refund share, so FULL_REFUND is not available.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-03205", "EV-TRIP-03205"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.refund.refund_before_rounding",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's framing of a 'quote' of 10.8 km misdescribes the fare model. The fare_breakdown records fare_model METERED with quoted_fare_sgd null, so no fixed price was promised at booking and the 10.8 km figure the rider cites is the platform's optimal-route estimate, not a contractual ceiling. The charge was computed by the meter for the distance actually driven, which is why the exposure falls to be measured by the POL-RD-02 recomputation above rather than by the difference between the metered total and a quote that was never issued.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-03205", "EV-TRIP-03205"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.components.fare_model",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Nothing in the pass-through layer enlarges the rider's recovery. The fare_breakdown carries no ERP or toll line at all (erp_lines total SGD 0.00, erp_gantries empty), no airport surcharge, a zero waiting_time_fee and no promo discount, so a POL-RD-09 correction adds nothing to the POL-RD-02 figure, and POL-RD-09(1) forbids any such line being added on top of the POL-RD-02 figure in any event.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-03205"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.erp_lines.total",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The metered billing tracks the trace, so there is no billing-integrity defect and no unbilled-distance shortfall. The fare_breakdown charges for 14.1 km against a trace length of 14.12 km, a difference of 0.02 km, which is inside POL-RD-04's 1.0 km threshold and supports no DRIVER_COMPENSATION claim. The driver's statement that 'the fare is what the meter says' is accurate as to the distance and time recorded, whatever the reason for the route taken.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-03205", "EV-GPS-03205"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09", "POL-RD-04"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.trace_distance_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "I do not press POL-RD-03 on this record, and I say so plainly: the counterparty statement attributes the extra distance to heavy traffic, but the bundle's traffic_advisory, EV-ADVIS-03205-01, is MISSING with admissibility weight 0.0 and issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, and has no payload. There is accordingly no advisory naming a road or segment the optimal route traverses, no validity window to test against the time the trace shows the vehicle would have reached that segment, and no matchable corridor departure and rejoinder, so the exoneration comparison in POL-RD-03 cannot be run and the traffic explanation reduces the measured excess by nothing. The case therefore falls to be decided on the POL-RD-02 arithmetic set out above, which is the driver's only real protection here.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-03205-01", "EV-GPS-03205"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.advisory_area.advisories",
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 3.55,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Both parties' positions converge on the same arithmetic, and the record decides the case. Deviation: the governing measurement is the trace, not the rounded copy. The GPS polyline (EV-GPS-03205, weight 1.0) runs 14.12 km between the recorded pickup and drop-off events; the booked optimal route (EV-TRIP-03205) is 10.8 km. That is an excess of 3.32 km, or 30.74%. Both POL-RD-01 establishment gates are cleared (over 20% of optimal and over 0.8 km absolute), so the route deviation is ESTABLISHED. It is not a MATERIAL deviation — 30.74% is below the 50% gate and 3.32 km is below the 8.0 km gate — so no POL-RD-06 driver-profile uplift or conduct referral arises, and on the driver profile the pattern test fails in any event (deviation_flags_90d = 1, and 1/172 = 0.006, both below threshold). The trace is not impaired for policy purposes: 111 fixes at 10-second intervals, 100% coverage, no gaps, max gap 0.0 seconds, so none of POL-RD-07(a)-(c) fires and no independent corroboration is required. The driver's own statement ('I took another road') concedes the route departure.\n\nDriver's traffic defence: the assertion that heavy traffic caused the detour is an external-traffic assertion. Under POL-RD-13 it is tested against the trip's traffic advisory and nothing else. EV-ADVIS-03205-01 is MISSING — weight_multiplier 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT — so there is no advisory naming a road the optimal route traverses and no validity window to test; the POL-RD-03 comparison cannot be run. The assertion therefore carries no weight under POL-RD-08 and reduces the measured excess by nothing. Because no party cites the missing identifier as the basis of an exculpatory claim (the driver expressly does not press POL-RD-03), this is a gap in the bundle, not an exculpatory clause invoked against a cited missing artifact, and it is not a POL-RD-10(5) escalation.\n\nNo exculpatory route applies: the chat log (EV-CHAT-03205) is empty, so no rider-requested detour under POL-RD-04; no pickup or drop-off amendment is recorded, so POL-RD-05 cannot run and the booked 10.8 km optimal stands; the vehicle is RYDE_X with solo_optimal_distance_km null, so POL-RD-12 does not apply; the fare model is METERED with quoted_fare_sgd null, so POL-RD-11 does not close off the distance remedy.\n\nRefund arithmetic under POL-RD-02: recomputed_fare = (3.80 base fare + 0.75 x 10.8 km + 0.28 x 14.6 min) x surge multiplier 1.0 read from the fare_breakdown + 0.80 platform fee + 0 ERP/tolls + 0 fixed surcharges + 0 waiting fee - 0 promo = 16.7880. charged_total = 20.30. Refund = 20.30 - 16.7880 = 3.5120, rounded UP to the nearest SGD 0.05 = SGD 3.55. This is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis floor and is 17.3% of the charge, far below the 90% full-refund share, so the outcome is PARTIAL_REFUND of SGD 3.55. No ERP, toll, airport surcharge or waiting-fee line exists on the fare breakdown, so no POL-RD-09 pass-through correction adds anything (and POL-RD-09(1) forbids adding one on top of the POL-RD-02 figure). No billing-integrity defect and no unbilled-distance shortfall exist: 14.1 km billed against 14.12 km traced, so no DRIVER_COMPENSATION is payable.\n\nConfidence: the deciding facts are carried by artifacts all at weight_multiplier 1.0 (GPS trace, trip record, fare breakdown), so the cap is 1.0; set at 0.90. The monetary effect of SGD 3.55 is below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so it executes automatically on issue under POL-GEN-05.",
    "referrals": []
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

