    "explanation": "To both parties: the GPS trace for trip TRP-03205 measures 14.12 km between the recorded pickup and drop-off, against a booked optimal route of 10.8 km. That is 3.32 km extra, or 30.74% — above both POL-RD-01 gates (over 20% and over 0.8 km), so a route deviation is established. The trace governs over the rounded trip_record copy, and it is complete: 111 fixes at 10-second intervals, 100.0% coverage, no gaps, so POL-RD-07 does not treat it as impaired and it establishes the deviation on its own. No rider-requested detour appears (the chat log holds zero messages), no pickup or drop-off relocation (every amendment field is null), and this is not a pooled trip, so the booked 10.8 km optimal stands as the comparator. The deviation is not MATERIAL (below 50% and below 8.0 km), so POL-RD-06 is not engaged. The driver accepts he 'took another road' and explains it by heavy traffic; under POL-RD-13 that excuse is tested against this trip's traffic advisory and nothing else, and the only advisory in the bundle, EV-ADVIS-03205-01, is MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0 and no payload — no road, no validity window, no corridor to compare. The assertion therefore carries no weight under POL-RD-08, reduces the measured excess by nothing, and is recorded as discarded; no traffic advisory was on file for this trip. The refund is arithmetic under POL-RD-02, computed on the optimal route. Recomputing the metered fare: (3.80 base fare + 0.75 x 10.8 km + 0.28 x 14.6 min) x surge 1.0, read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier, + 0.80 platform fee = 16.788. Charged_total was 20.30, so the refund is 20.30 - 16.788 = 3.512, rounded up to the nearest SGD 0.05 = SGD 3.55. Mr Koh, that is below the SGD 6.50 you contested: your figure treats the 10.8 km optimal estimate as a fixed quote, but this was a metered fare (fare_model METERED, quoted_fare_sgd null), so the correct measure is the recomputed metered fare, not the gap between the total and a quote that was never issued. The refund is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis floor and only 17.3% of the charged total, far below the 90% full-refund share. There are no ERP, toll or surcharge lines to correct separately (erp total 0.00, no gantries), and no phantom line, so no POL-RD-09 correction or billing-integrity referral arises. The driver_profile shows no repeat-deviation pattern (deviation_flags_90d 1, far below both POL-RD-06 thresholds), so no FULL_REFUND uplift and no driver-conduct referral. No POL-RD-10 escalation ground fires: identifiers match across all three artifacts, timestamps agree, the trace is unimpaired, and every charge line has a counterpart in the trace and trip record. The monetary effect of SGD 3.55 is below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold and will be executed automatically on issue."
